%% showcase: gantt axisFormat with ISO week numbers
%% prose: `%V` is the ISO 8601 week and `%G` its week-numbering year, so the first ticks of January read `2025-W52`, then `2026-W01`… `%U` and `%W` count Sunday- and Monday-based weeks from the calendar year instead, starting at week 0.
gantt
    title Quarter plan
    dateFormat YYYY-MM-DD
    axisFormat %G-W%V
    tickInterval 1week
    weekday monday
    section Plan
    Discovery   :d1, 2025-12-22, 2w
    Design      :d2, after d1, 3w
    section Build
    Build       :b1, after d2, 4w
